== Effects ==
* Increases all [[Attributes|stats]] while Isaac's active item is fully charged:
** +0.25 [[speed]].
** +0.75 [[range]].
** {{dlc|nr}} +0.50 [[tear falling speed]].
** +0.20 [[tears]].
** +0.10 [[shot speed]].
** +0.50 [[damage]].
** +1 [[luck]].

== Notes ==
* The trinket creates no effect if Isaac has no active item.
* {{dlc|nr}} Active items that are reusable indefinitely without a charge bar, such as {{i|How to Jump}}, will allow Vibrant Bulb's effects to be permanent (until the active item is swapped out).
* Vibrant Bulb is slightly less than half as powerful as {{t|Dim Bulb|n}}; however, its effects are active more often.
* {{i|Glowing Hourglass|nr}}, when used, will not make the Vibrant Bulb inactive and will still provide the bonus until it has one bar of charge.
* Having additional charge beyond full with {{i|The Battery}} does not provide an additional bonus. It does give an advantage however, since using the fully charged item once still provides Vibrant Bulb's effect.
* If two active items are held ({{i|Schoolbag|n}}), the one currently active must be at full charge for the trinket to take effect (the other one doesn't need to be fully charged).
* {{dlc+|r}} Vibrant Bulb produces no effect with active items in consumable slots, e.g. {{c|Tainted Apollyon}}'s {{i|Abyss|n}} or {{c|Tainted Bethany}}'s {{i|Lemegeton}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} If {{c|Bethany}} or {{c|Tainted Bethany}} are holding enough soul/red hearts to charge her current active item, the Vibrant Bulb will be active, even if there are no regular charges.{{dlc-}}
** If the active item is fully charged only with soul/blood charges and no regular charges, Vibrant Bulb and Dim Bulb can be both active at the same time if Isaac holds both of the trinkets.

== Synergies ==
* {{A|Golden Trinket|r+}} / {{i|Mom's Box|r+}}: Having either doubles the stat increases. Having both triples them.

